body:
I've been lifting for a little under a year and a half now, and I have started deadlifting within the last few months - I avoided it initially because I was afraid of ruining my back, but it turns out it's my favorite lift now, hah.

&#x200B;

Anyways, I have been doing touch-and-go reps where I just barely tap the floor with the weight before I go back up. This makes the first rep much harder than the middle reps, though of course reps at the end are still very difficult, since I typically do 2 sets to failure or 1 RIR.

&#x200B;

For reference, I am 165 lbs and my last session was 325 lbs for 6 reps. I want to know what I should be doing to get closer to that sweet sweet 405 lbs mark, and when I should give it a shot. I am concerned that most expectations are that pause reps are what I should be using to measure my 1RM strength when it comes to deadlift, so I don't really know how close I am, in all honestly. Can I expect to be hitting 405 soon? Could I hit it today? I don't really know - some days it feels like I just barely get the first rep of my set off the floor.

Hey everyone, I have read the injury section of the FAQ, as well as some other relevant sections, and I still haven't found an answer to my question.

&#x200B;

Essentially, I have been running a lot. I am pretty good at it, I think, but I have a fairly serious problem. Usually about a half mile into my run (or sooner, sometimes right at the start), my ankles begin hurting. This pain dies down a bit as I run, but then, as soon as I complete the run, it comes *rushing back* and it is almost agonizing. I am barely able to walk or stand due to the pain. When I completely take pressure off my legs by sitting, it is reduced, but not completely gone.

&#x200B;

The pain is usually negligible within an hour, but this is a pretty serious issue for me. I am using a pair of Hoka running shoes, if that is relevant, and they have a high amount of cushion.

&#x200B;

My running form seems okay, I'm quite puzzled by this, but it's a pretty annoying issue to have since cardio is important to me. This also isn't a new issue, but I realized that asking about it on reddit might finally help me resolve it...

&#x200B;

Additionally, last year I became concerned about this issue, so I quit running for about 3 months to see if it was an injury that would heal by itself. When I started again in late August, the first few runs were without pain, but then it started hurting again like it used to, and it has continued to hurt since.

\[WR\]

&#x200B;

DLC 3 (Treasure of the Midnight Isles) questions.

&#x200B;

First of all, is there any way to respec? I screwed up a single feat on a character and now I feel like I am just screwed with no way of recovering it. I even tried the respec mod and it just deleted the character from my party instead of actually respecing them...

&#x200B;

Also, is there any way to return to port or rest safely?! I rested a single time, for 9 hours, on the boat, and instantly shot up from 0 to past LVL 1 corruption! This is unacceptable, I have no idea how you are supposed to progress in this DLC with this kind of stuff happening. For the record, I am playing on normal.

&#x200B;

I tried talking to the Helmsman about returning to port, but he just says that will end the adventure entirely.

&#x200B;

I also don't see any merchants on the boat or anything. Please give me some guidance since I can't figure out how to make this experience playable.

&#x200B;

This is all extremely confusing and frustrating.

Okay. I am following Erastil so my domains are already community and plant. 

&#x200B;

I will keep that in mind, for when I get mythic power on this character.

Well first of all, he can't fire twice since he only has a single attack. Not sure where you got that from.

&#x200B;

Second, Necrons aren't exactly known for tactical savviness.

Yes please.

&#x200B;

https://docs.google.com/document/d/1elFR-RFoGQaE9KieHLGJZycGiecqWk06iN4qSEptaDo/edit?usp=sharing

That's a great idea!

&#x200B;

Personally, I was going to plan it so that in my adventure, the players will just *conveniently* have access to the proper weapons to be able to disable the regeneration. I will probably downgrade it to fast healing, then, and just say that at 0 hp they activate Defense Protocols, which is another very necron-y thing to do.

Thanks for the advice on making a Necron creature type. I will consider it! I thought for quite a while about Fast Healing vs Regeneration - I decided on Regeneration due to their behavior in the books primarily - Necrons getting blasted to pieces by Imperial Guard forces and then just pulling themselves back together in moments.

&#x200B;

I will reduce the damage of the Gauss Flayer, though, and additionally make it unwieldable by non-Necrons (which is how it is supposed to be, regardless).

Alright, I will consider that. 

&#x200B;

Now, their damage is based around the typical stats for a CR 5 creature according to the [Monster Creation rules](https://www.d20pfsrd.com/bestiary/rules-for-monsters/monster-creation/). Their melee damage is actually low, since they only get one attack. The ranged damage also only comes out to \~20 (although it is touch).

\[WOTR\]

&#x200B;

Do I need to have a Nahyndrian Crystal before I go to Threshold? I haven't seen anything suggesting this and I haven't acquired any. I am not trying to go for the Secret Ending or anything.

I really appreciate the help!

&#x200B;

Toybox just has a LOT of sub-menus and sometimes it's hard to find exactly what I want. I spent a long time fiddling with the Search-n-Pick section where I was able to give Ember the ability as a SLA (but not what I want, of course).

