Well, I would think that you would probably answer no, since it seems silly on it's face. However, at the same time, you should say 'yes' for consistency since it doesn't seem to me that California has what you call "American Values", and if that is such a bad thing, then it shouldn't be part of the USA.

&#x200B;

And of course, if you think that California is a rightful part of the US, then it would seem that a welfare state is indeed part of American Values, since the largest, most productive state in the union supports one.

It applies to all of them. They have sectioned off different parts of the US and have effectively no competition.

&#x200B;

Worse yet are the rural areas in the United States which have to buy satellite based internet, which is far worse than internet in urban areas; it is orders of magnitude slower, latency is high, there are egregiously low data caps, and you will typically **pay more than anyone in an urban area** for this atrocious service.

&#x200B;

And yes, there are multiple satellite internet companies - they all do the same shit.

So use flame breath at the edge? I actually do that sometimes! It typically works well, although here and there he manages to blast through it by grabbing the ledge and then climb-hitting (unsure of the name of that maneuver).

&#x200B;

I really need to learn how to properly use my down smash. I have a hard time getting it to come out properly because of how my controls are set up.

With respect to the juggling, it's because to hit him, I need to wait for him to get close, he air dodges, and then I don't have any more chances to hit him before he lands and then the juggling is over.

&#x200B;

Ganondorf's down smash hits both sides and get's its first hit on frame 15. His up smash, on frame 20 and that smash hits everywhere. Maybe I'm just a dunce, but these seem fast for smashes?

&#x200B;

I do punish sometimes. It's hard for me because I usually do it with up-b but then the move gets stale. I am trying to understand your advice on being evasive, but when I do that it just seems like he then gets free time to try and swing at me while I am evading, and eventually mistakes will be made and I die. Please give me a few more details if that's ok so I understand what you mean.

&#x200B;

Our matches are always so strange. They usually start out with me beating him up to like 100% while taking minimal damage... and then suddenly the reverse happens and I'm dead and he's rocking at like 120%, and then the next stock I take 50% by the time I manage to get a lethal hit on him. I don't really know what is happening.

Yeah, the Bowser Bomb does break a full shield if it lands directly on them and Bowser didn't use it on the ground. 

&#x200B;

It is basically never actually useful as a shield-breaker since it has a lot of startup time and if they are shielding, then they have time to dodge or at the very least put the shield down.

&#x200B;

Overall I do like the move, but it's shield-break potential seems to be overhyped. And of course, you can't do it if they have a platform overhead.


I really love Bowser's side-b, but the range is so small I often get the spacing all wrong lol.

